      "houseRulesSections": "Checking in and out: Check-in after 4:00 PM, Checkout before 10:00 AM, Self check-in with keypad, During your stay: 8 guests maximum, Pets allowed, Quiet hours, No parties or events, Commercial photography allowed, No smoking"
    },
    {
      "id": "HIGHLIGHTS_DEFAULT",
      "highlights": "Self check-in, Mountain and valley views, At-home coffee"
    },
    {
      "id": "DESCRIPTION_DEFAULT",
      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "Just minutes from gold medal fishing and water sports recreation, this modern mountain home was custom built to capture 360 degree views. The living areas and full kitchen are on the upper floor to take advantage of these dramatic alpine views .With 4 spacious bedrooms with private bathrooms , two masters with soaking tub , luxury bedding and all the high end confort you appreciate during a relaxing vacation.  Bring your family and friends to this beautiful resort style private property.<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />Welcome to The Glass House in Basalt, Colorado—a luxurious mountain retreat offering breathtaking 360⁰ views and an unbeatable location just minutes from the stunning Ruedi Reservoir. Perfect for friends and family gatherings, this unique property combines modern design with Western charm, delivering the feel of a small boutique hotel in the heart of the Rockies.  <br /><br />**Property Highlights:**  <br />- 360⁰ Panoramic Views: Floor-to-ceiling windows provide uninterrupted vistas of the surrounding mountains and forests, ensuring an awe-inspiring backdrop from every angle.  <br />- Modern Western Décor: The stylish interior blends contemporary elegance with rustic touches, creating a warm and inviting space.  <br />- Open Concept Living: The seamless layout features high ceilings and expansive living areas, perfect for connecting with loved ones.  <br /><br /> **Features & Amenities:**  <br />- Spacious Bedrooms: Thoughtfully designed with plush bedding and en-suite bathrooms for ultimate comfort and privacy.  <br />- Gourmet Kitchen: Fully equipped with top-of-the-line appliances and a large island—ideal for cooking meals together.  <br />- Outdoor Perfection: Enjoy the expansive deck with a hot tub, outdoor dining space, and lounge chairs—perfect for soaking up the mountain air and starry nights.  <br />- Boutique Hotel Feel: With its sleek design and luxurious touches, the property offers the comfort of home and the sophistication of a high-end retreat.  <br /><br />**Important Details:**  <br />- Maximum Capacity: The property accommodates a maximum of 8 guests at all times due to HOA regulations.  <br />- Septic System: Please note that the home operates on a septic system, which limits its capacity to handle larger groups. For this reason, it’s essential to adhere to the guest limit for everyone’s comfort and convenience.  <br /><br /> **Location:**  <br />Nestled in the charming town of Basalt, The Glass House is minutes from Ruedi Reservoir, where you can enjoy fishing, paddle boarding, and scenic picnics. Aspen’s vibrant cultural scene and world-class skiing are just a short drive away, offering the perfect balance of adventure and relaxation.  <br /><br /> **Additional Perks:**  <br />- High-Speed Wi-Fi: Stay connected with reliable internet access throughout the property.  <br />- Entertainment System: Host movie nights with a flat-screen TV and premium sound system.  <br />- Private Parking: Ample parking space for guests’ convenience.  <br /><br /> **Perfect for Gatherings:**  <br />Whether you're planning a reunion, a group getaway, or a relaxing retreat, The Glass House provides the ideal setting to create lasting memories—while maintaining its serene, eco-friendly atmosphere.  <br /><br />Book now to experience this exceptional mountain escape, where luxury meets natural beauty and adventure is just outside your door.<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />We will share the code to enter the house through Airbnb Messages a few days prior your arrival.<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />4x4 Vehicle Required year round. Fees may apply due to HOA. <br />Vehicles traveling uphill yield to vehicles traveling downhill.  Please don’t start to drive up the big hill if there is a car at the top, about to come down.  Make sure you look before proceeding up the road.  <br />*Note this is opposite standard driving protocol.   Best way to get up the big hill, winter or summer, is to use 4WD, a low gear, and go slowly.  <br /><br />Small dogs allowed with previous authorization and a fee of $350.<br />If there is any damage the fee will escalate.<br />Cleanings Services upon request, Tenant pays for extra cleanings."
      }
