      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "Real XII Century Monastery portion converted into a luxury unique loft in the Duomo area of Milano<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />Original Ex-Monastery converted and finely renovated into a luxury apartment for your best stay in the heart of the city, Duomo area. Zone 1.<br /><br /><br />The \"Monastery of San Simone\" was founded and developed between the 12th and 16th centuries. The Monastery was the Milanese seat of the Order of the Humiliated, one of the spiritual movements that arose in contrast to the relaxed customs and widespread wealth often flaunted by the clergy, advocating a return to a more austere, frugal life. Initially condemned as heretics, they were reinstated by the papacy at the beginning of the 13th century until their definitive suppression in 1570 following the Council of Trent by Pope Pius V.<br />The “Monastery of San Simone” was located between today's Corso di Porta Ticinese, Largo Carrobbio and Via Cesare Correnti. It consisted of a central building with a large courtyard with main entrance from street number 12 of Corso di Porta Ticinese from a cemetery behind and a church, today's deconsecrated church of San Simone located in Via Cesare Correnti. The main activity of the Monastery was the processing and dyeing of wool and fabrics, taking advantage of the water of the Vetra river that flowed in the immediate vicinity.<br />After the suppression of the Order of the Humiliated, the Monastery of San Simone was divided among multiple lay owners, while keeping its original main courtyard intact over the centuries with access from number 12 of Corso di Porta Ticinese with the scenery of the Basilica of San Lorenzo and its Romanesque columns.<br /><br /><b>Registration number</b><br />IT015146C2D75KNMWC"
      }
