    {
      "id": "DESCRIPTION_DEFAULT",
      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "Dine at a wood-carved table under exposed beams, reflected on a rare collection of ancient convex mirrors, before taking a stroll on secret narrow pedestrian streets once inhabited by artists and poets. Chill out in a charming living room with a fireplace, saddle-stitched leather couch, and shutter doors opening to a balcony with plants. Rest in a Balinese king-size canopy bed under an ancient coffered ceiling. Refined furnishings, wide spaces, and a pleasant scent of wellness will make you feel at home in an outstanding setting in the most characteristic and special neighborhood of Milan's city center.<br /><br />If you contact me, through Airbnb or my phone number, I will always reply within a few seconds<br /><br />The lovely pedestrian Brera district is like a romantic village out of time in the heart of Milan. Once inhabited by artists and poets, the red-light culture and artistic vocation left a very particular energy. Today it's a new center of design, fashion, and luxury while retaining its authentic atmosphere. Walking through its narrow secret streets, visiting Palazzo di Brera and smelling the bohemian atmosphere are just some of the peculiarities that make Brera a jewel to be enjoyed.<br /><br />The apartment is served by all public transport:<br /><br />- 150 meters from the Lanza-Piccolo Teatro metro stop (green line)<br /><br />- 300 meters from the Cairoli metro stop (red line)<br /><br />- 200 meters from the Via Ponte Vetero tram stop (lines 2, 12 and 14)<br /><br />- 800 meters from Cadorna Station where trains depart for Malpensa Airport (Malpensa Express)<br /><br />- 3 metro stops from Porta Garibaldi Station<br /><br />- 4 metro stops from the Central Station<br /><br />- 80 meters from the taxi station on Via Mercato<br /><br />- car and bike sharing everywhere nearby<br /><br />———————————————<br />The apartment is served by all public transport:<br /><br />- 150 meters from Lanza-Piccolo Teatro metro station (green line)<br /><br />- 300 meters from Cairoli metro station (red line)<br /><br />- 200 meters from the Via Ponte Vetero tram stop (lines 2, 12, and 14)<br /><br />- 800 meters from Cadorna Station where trains leave for Malpensa Airport (Malpensa Express)<br /><br />- 3 metro stops from Porta Garibaldi Station<br /><br />- 4 metro stops from Central Station<br /><br />- 80 meters from the taxi station on Via Mercato<br /><br />- car and bike sharing anywhere nearby<br /><br />INFORMATION AND INSTRUCTIONS FOR CHECK-IN AND CHECK-OUT<br /><br />CHECK IN<br />Password: FLEXIBILITY!<br />The Host guarantees the possibility of checking in at any time of the day or night at no extra cost.<br />Normally the apartment is available to check in from noon (12:00 pm).<br />Any availability of the apartment before noon will be duly communicated by the Host at least the day before.<br />In any case, Guests are always allowed to leave their luggage and personal belongings in the apartment (or in a safe place) even before the agreed check-in time (as well as after the check-out time, as specified below), at any time of the day or night.<br /><br />Guests usually agree with the Host, before their arrival, on the approximate time.<br /><br />1)    Morning check-in<br />Upon their arrival at Via San Carpoforo n. 4, Guests can ask the doorman of the next building (Via San Carpoforo n. 6), whose name is Shiran, to call the maid (Emi) who is always available at home.<br />The doorman Shiran is always on site Monday-Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 1:00 p.m.<br />Guests can also press button no. 7 on the intercom: There is always someone at home ready to welcome them.<br />The Host lives in the same building and ensures his constant presence and availability in receiving guests upon their arrival.<br /><br />2)    Check-in at different times<br />In the event that Guests arrive at any time of the day or night, it will be advisable to notify the Host in advance and agree on an approximate arrival time.<br />