      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "Comfort, convenience, privacy, and security underlie the traditional tropical Asian aesthetics and tranquility of Villa Kilau Indah. Kilau indah translates as beautiful shimmer, which is precisely what occurs at sunset on most days at this property. For guests staying more than 14 nights we offer free pick up and drop anywhere on Bali. Our cook, Dewi, speaks English and prepares Western and Indonesian breakfast, lunch, and dinner (gluten-free on request). Guest pay for groceries, no surcharges.<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />The villa offers 3 spacious bedrooms, each with a private ensuite bathroom and handmade canopied king size bed. The master suite includes a large creative working space facing the terrace, pool, and sea. The massive open living/dining room and kitchen offers every amenity and adjoins an airy and cool veranda facing the pool and sea. Air conditioning and ceiling fans are in every space.  We provide laundry service at no charge (the laundry is not in the villa). The clear sunlit infinity pool is 15 by 6 meters with a large stone deck and pavilion. The villa sits on a black volcanic sand beach of the Bali Sea.<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />The villa, pool, and large garden are entirely and privately yours. The beach is public but you will see no throngs of tourists; only a very few others like you and local fishermen. Guests are always let in by staff. We do not operate a key lock box.<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />We speak English, Indonesian, and Spanish. <br /><br />The rural setting of the villa includes daily religious observances by local Hindus and Moslems alike within earshot of the villa, though not overwhelmingly so. During the annual 2-day Eid observance the mosque is much more active than ordinary, though through the month of Ramadan, there is considerably more activity."
