      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "Welcome to Villa Murakami, a Japanese-inspired house with three beautifully designed bedrooms and a spacious living room offering stunning ocean views. Enjoy the refreshing pool, walk  200 m to the beach, drive 7 min to Playa Hermosa (the best multilevel surf spot in the area) or 15 min to Santa Teresa. Your stay also includes beach gear, and a concierge manager is ready to assist with rentals, horseback riding, or a personal chef. Experience unforgettable coastal bliss at Villa Murakami!<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />Villa Murakami seamlessly blends comfort and elegance, offering three beautifully designed bedrooms for a restful escape. Two of the bedrooms feature king-size beds, while the third is equipped with two  single beds, making it perfect for families or groups. Each bedroom includes a dedicated workspace and ample clothing storage for your convenience.<br /><br />The  living area is seamlessly merged with the kitchen, creating an inviting open space for socializing and relaxation. The living room features a comfortable sitting bench-style couch and a traditional low Japanese tea-style table that seats six, perfect for shared meals or quiet moments. The kitchen extends into a stylish bar area with seating for five, making it an excellent spot for casual dining or enjoying drinks.<br /><br />Step outside to unwind by the refreshing pool and outdoor table.<br />Perched atop a hill in the serene village of Manzanillo, just a short distance from Santa Teresa, this peaceful paradise offers breathtaking views and a tranquil retreat.<br /><br />Housekeeping services, including pool and home cleaning, are provided twice a week, with additional services available upon request. Experience the ultimate beachside getaway at Villa Murakami, where every detail is designed for your comfort and enjoyment.<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />At Villa Murakami, guests have full and exclusive access to the entire property, ensuring complete privacy and a seamless stay. This includes:<br /><br />The Villa: Enjoy all three bedrooms, the open-concept living room, and the fully equipped kitchen with a bar area.<br />Outdoor Spaces: Relax by the private pool and take in the breathtaking views from the outdoor seating areas.<br />Beach Gear Available: To enhance your beach experience, we provide beach essentials, including towels, tent and chairs. Feel free to take them along for a relaxing day by the ocean.<br />Ping Pong Table: Guests can enjoy a ping pong table for friendly matches. However, please note that it is sensitive to rain and prolonged sun exposure—kindly fold and store it after use to maintain its condition.<br />Parking: on-site parking is available for guests traveling with a rental car.<br />Wi-Fi & Workspaces: Each bedroom features a dedicated workspace, making it convenient for remote work or personal projects.<br /><br /><br />Whether you're here for relaxation or adventure, Villa Murakami offers a serene and fully equipped retreat for an unforgettable stay.<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />Housekeeping & Pool Maintenance: Regular cleaning services are included twice a week, covering both the house and pool area. Additional cleaning can be arranged upon request.<br />Wi-Fi & Workspaces: The villa is equipped with Starlink Wi-Fi, and each bedroom features a dedicated workspace (please, use Starlink Ext in the Bedroom #3 if the service will be breaking)<br />Hilltop Location: Villa Murakami is perched on a hill in the peaceful village of Manzanillo, you need to go down from the hill to the beach and go back the same way. A rental car or ATV is recommended for easy access to nearby beaches and Santa Teresa.<br />Family & Group Friendly: The villa is ideal for families or groups, offering a mix of king and single beds, spacious common areas, and plenty of entertainment options.<br />Eco-Friendly Design: The villa is designed with sustainability in mind, featuring natural ventilation and locally sourced materials that blend harmoniously with the surrounding landscape."
