      "houseRulesSections": "Checking in and out: Check-in after 3:00 PM, Checkout before 11:00 AM, Self check-in with lockbox, During your stay: 4 guests maximum, No pets, Quiet hours, No parties or events, Commercial photography allowed, No smoking, Additional rules, Before you leave: Turn things off, Return keys"
    },
    {
      "id": "LOCATION_DEFAULT",
      "lat": 8.582480464143567,
      "lng": -83.38181162055962,
      "subtitle": "Puerto Jiménez, Provincia de Puntarenas, Costa Rica",
      "title": "Where you’ll be"
    },
    {
      "id": "HIGHLIGHTS_DEFAULT",
      "highlights": "Top 5% of homes, 50-min drive to Parque Nacional Corcovado, Self check-in"
    },
    {
      "id": "DESCRIPTION_DEFAULT",
      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "This magical fairytale treehouse is nestled high in the treetops of the jungle, 15 minutes from Puerto Jimenez—the gateway to Corcovado National Park. This escape offers the perfect blend of adventure and comfort. With a river bordering the property, scenic walking trails, and abundant wildlife, it provides an immersive experience in nature. Exploring the jungle, listening to the sounds of the river, or simply relaxing in the treetops, this treehouse promises an unforgettable getaway.<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />A 5-minute walk from the Treehouse brings you to the serene Golfito Bay, where kayaks are available for your explorations. Paddle along the calm waters, surrounded by the beauty of nature. Afterward, relax in the suspended hammock, soaking in the soothing sounds of the jungle, or unwind in the bath while spotting playful monkeys nearby. For a truly refreshing experience, enjoy an outdoor shower under a canopy of stars.<br /><br />When it’s time to retreat indoors, the A/C and modern amenities ensure your comfort in this tranquil haven. The Treehouse offers the perfect blend of rustic charm and luxury, making it an ideal escape from the world.<br /><br />Explore scenic walking trails that wind through the jungle, teeming with wildlife. The property is frequently visited by three species of monkeys, offering a truly immersive wildlife experience right outside your door. Nearby, the breathtaking Corcovado National Park awaits, offering unforgettable tours and opportunities to explore one of the most biodiverse places on Earth.<br /><br />Take time to enjoy the wonders of Golfito Bay, where vibrant marine life, including fish, whales, and dolphins, thrive in the pristine waters. Just a short distance away lies the magnificent Gulfo Dulce, Central America’s largest natural estuary, fed by 22 rivers and home to a vast array of species.<br /><br />This magical treehouse has everything you need to experience the wonders of the jungle in style and serenity. Located in the heart of the Osa Peninsula, it offers the perfect base to explore, relax, and immerse yourself in the natural beauty and wildlife of this extraordinary region. Whether you seek adventure or relaxation, this treehouse is the ultimate gateway.<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />There are two ways to get to the Treehouse, each offering its own unique experience. The first option is to fly into Puerto Jimenez Airport with Sansa Airlines, offering a stunningly scenic flight over the lush landscapes of the Osa Peninsula. Once you arrive, the cabin is just a 15-minute drive or taxi ride away. The second option is to fly into San José International Airport, rent a car, and embark on a beautiful 5-hour drive through the Costa Rican countryside. Be sure to stop at the famous Crocodile Bridge in Tarcoles—it’s a must-see along the way! Whether you choose to drive or fly, a two-wheel drive vehicle is more than enough to navigate the journey with ease.<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />Since the property borders a river, it serves as a natural wildlife corridor, providing a habitat for an incredible variety of animals. This unique location means that the wildlife on the property is abundant and diverse, offering an unforgettable opportunity for nature lovers and wildlife enthusiasts.<br /><br />Some of the remarkable animals that have been spotted here include Sloths, Coatimundis, and Tamanduas. You may also catch a glimpse of a River Otter gliding through the water or a rat snake slinking across the trails. The skies above are often graced by the majestic Scarlet Macaw, Roseate Spoonbill, and even the occasional Black Hawk soaring overhead. At night, the sounds of the jungle come alive with the hoots of a Spectacle Owl or the rustling of a Kinkajou in the trees.<br /><br />The property is also home to a variety of reptiles, including the River Turtle, Red-Tailed Boa, Cat-Eyed Snake, “Jesus Christ” lizard, also known as the basilisk, and the infamous Ferdelance Snake . Mammals like the Jaguarundi, Opossum, and Porcupine roam the trails, while Capuchin Monkeys, Howler Monkeys, and Squirrel Monkeys swing through the canopy. You might also be lucky enough to spot an Armadillo, Red-Eyed Tree frog, Skunk, or even an Ocelot at night as you explore the Jungle.<br /><br />The diversity of bird species is equally impressive, with the Chestnut-mandibled Toucan, Tinamou, Acari, Amazon Parrot, and Boat-Billed Heron among the many avian residents. Geckos and Tanagers can be seen darting about, while Green Iguanas often bask in the sun. The lush jungle is alive with an ever-changing mix of creatures, each more fascinating than the last.<br /><br />With such an extraordinary array of wildlife, the property offers a truly immersive experience. Take a walk, keep your eyes peeled, and see what you can find in this vibrant natural paradise!"
      }
