      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "A traditional little palace within 10 minutes walk from the entrance of the Medina. The house is close to a pharmacy and grocery store. <br />A PRIVATE HOUSE YOU WON'T SHARE WITH OTHER GUESTS. <br />Price depends on the number of guests.<br />Wifi available.<br />Traditional meals can be served by Hayat who is there to help and clean when you request it. If you wish to have more privacy, tell her.<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />This little palace was built by wealthy merchants of Fez in the 17th century.  The house is built on a small hill overlooking the walled city and allows a panoramic view of the Medina from the terrace.<br /><br />The Medina is not accessible to vehicles because of the narrow streets. The house is within 10 minutes walk from the entrance of the Medina. <br /><br />Two suites are available on the first floor and a bedroom on the second floor. Each bedroom has a double bed, a dressing room and a bathroom. A bathroom is also available on the ground floor. <br /><br />Hayat is at your disposal. She can serve you meals and you can discuss the menu with her the day before. If you wish, meals can be prepared in the kitchen so that you can learn some Moroccan recipes, ask her, she is an excellent cook. If you do not want her to prepare the meals in the kitchen of the house, please let her know. Hayat also does the cleaning and can do your room if you ask her. If you want more privacy, let her know and lock the front door.  <br /><br />This is an \"open minded\" place,  respectful of all people.<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />The number of guests having access to the house cannot be above the number appearing on the reservation (see AirBnB regulations) <br /><br />Guests have access to the entire house. Access to the bedrooms depends on the number of guests<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />1. Breakfast (60 DH / person. Approx 6€) and dinner can be ordered (140 DH / person. Approx 14€) a day in advance with an endless choice of traditional Moroccan food that you will not find in restaurants.<br /><br />2. The house is open for rent in winter. December to March can be cold in Morocco and large houses or palaces cannot be fully heated because of the open patio. Bedrooms have reversible air conditioning (heating). The living room and the dining room have a gas heater.<br />Air conditioners must be turned off when leaving the bedrooms ! Thank you"
      }
