    {
      "id": "DESCRIPTION_DEFAULT",
      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "CIN (National Identification Code): IT027042C2C9CK4ZLY<br /><br />\"Mysteries of the East is located on the first floor of a building with a magnificent location overlooking the water and enjoys a spectacular view at the crossroads of the canals between the Scuola Grande and the Abbazia della Misericordia. You will feel captivated by this particularly evocative glimpse and will feel as if you are floating on the water, a hidden spectator of an exciting parade of boats of all kinds. Here, in total relaxation, you will be able to appreciate the alliance between art and nature.<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />The apartment, which has undergone a complete renovation, features refined spaces with attention to detail, enhanced with refined furnishings and references to the link between Venice and the East. The effect is that of a particularly cocoon-like and comfortable location, illuminated by spectacular reflections of water that follow one another from dawn to dusk and that create an intimate and romantic atmosphere that is particularly appreciated by couples.<br />It is accessed from a common lobby, with a single flight of stairs.<br />The entrance separates the sleeping area on the left, where the main bedroom and bathroom are located, from the living area on the right, with the bright living room and kitchenette. This is followed by the second bedroom, separated by a characteristic Indonesian wooden door and embellished with a curtain that encloses the walk-in closet. <br />The rooms are air-conditioned and there is a Wi-Fi connection. <br />The kitchenette is well equipped, with induction stoves, electric/microwave ovens, a dishwasher, a coffee machine and various other small appliances.<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />The property is located in the Cannaregio neighborhood, near the foundations of Santa Caterina. It is accessed from a typical Venetian courtyard, equipped with a dock for boats and motorboats. It is very convenient due to its proximity to the main tourist attractions, Strada Nuova – a shopping street – and Calle della Misericordia, which is renowned for its nightlife and its 'bacari' (taverns), as well as its proximity to San Marco and Rialto. Easily accessible from the \"Ca' d'Oro\" vaporetto stop and the \"Fondamenta Nove\" Alilaguna stop that connects the city with the airport.<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />OTHER THINGS TO BEAR IN MIND<br />The price includes all gas, electricity, waste collection, etc. as well as bedding and towels.<br /><br />ARRIVALS AND DEPARTURES<br />Check-in, by appointment, is from 3:00 p.m. to 7:00 p.m., unless otherwise agreed.<br />Check-out is at 10 a.m., unless otherwise agreed.<br />Check-in is not possible on the following days of the year:<br />December 24/25/26/31 and January 1.<br /><br />EXTRA COSTS:<br />• \tTOURIST TAX, introduced by the municipality of Venice, is an extra to be paid on arrival, at the following rates (subject to changes in the law):<br />Full price €4.00 per person per night (maximum 5 nights)<br />Reduced price €2.00 for children from 10 to 16 years (not yet 16 years old) per night (maximum 5 nights)<br />Free for children under 10 years of age. <br /><br />• \tSUPPLEMENT FOR LATE ARRIVALS: there is a supplement of €30.00 to be paid on arrival, for agreed arrivals after 7:00 p.m. and until 9:00 p.m.<br /><br />ITALIAN LAWS AND REGULATIONS<br />Italian law requires the identification of all guests: for this reason, identity documents will be required upon arrival.<br /><br />INSIDE THE HOUSE:<br />Smoking is prohibited;<br />Pets are not allowed;<br />Parties and events are prohibited;<br />We ask that you consult the book in the accommodation for instructions on appliances, emergency numbers, various information, etc.<br /><br /><b>Registration number</b><br />IT027042C2C9CK4ZLY"
      }
