      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "Escape to this unique Kukama-themed loft-cottage, nestled along the river in Padrecocha, a peaceful village just 20 minutes from Iquitos. Home to Kukama, Yagua, and Bora families, the community offers a deep connection to Amazonian life.<br /><br />Immerse yourself in the rich culture of the Amazon—learn and practice traditional medicine and its ceremonies, hike jungle trails, navigate the Momón, Nanay, and Amazon rivers, spot pink dolphins, fish for piranhas, and swim in the refreshing waters!<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />Loft - Cottage overlooking the Nanay river, 20 minutes by boat trip from Iquitos city.<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />Full access<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />Discover Padrecocha – A Gateway to the Amazon<br /><br />Just 20 minutes from Iquitos, Padrecocha is a vibrant riverside village accessible by public boat from the Bellavista-Nanay port. Home to Kukama, Bora, Yagua, and mestizo communities, it offers a deep cultural experience and a perfect base for exploring the Nanay, Momón, and Amazon rivers. Public boats operate daily from 5:00 AM to 7:00 PM, with on-call express boats available anytime.<br /><br />What Can You Do in Padrecocha?<br /><br />    Amazonian Traditional Medicine – Learn and practice ancient healing traditions, sacred plant knowledge, ceremonies, and special diets.<br />    Cultural Experiences – Visit Malocas (community centers) to explore indigenous history, music, dance, and crafts.<br />    Jungle Adventures – Take guided hikes or camping trips in the vast communal reserve, with expert local guides leading the way.<br />    Wildlife & River Tours – Fish for piranhas in the Momón River, spot pink dolphins in the Amazon, or visit the butterfly farm, rescue center, insectarium, and aquarium.<br />    Customized Boat Excursions – Enjoy private half-day or full-day trips on the Momón, Nanay, and Amazon rivers with a bilingual guide.<br /><br />Escape the bustle of Iquitos while staying close to everything. Come and experience the magic of Padrecocha—you're always welcome!"
