        "htmlText": "Palo Estate will transport you to a world of relaxation and inspiration. The home is surrounded by serene desert landscapes and is filled with a handpicked collection of one-of-a-kind furniture and decor. Look out any window and you’ll be greeted by the warm hues of the high desert. Step outside into the custom built heated pool or hot tub that overlook the valley and national park.<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />Built in 1955, this custom-built home exemplifies the rustic, cabin-like feel of many homes built in this area in the mid 20th century. The interior renovations celebrate the rustic and handcrafted nature of the original build.<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />Guests have full access to the entire property including the 5 acres that stretch to the south of the home. Guests can also enjoy the pool and hot tub<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />Please note: Hot tub heating is free. We do not charge for that. But if you would like to heat the pool, we charge $195 per night. This charge is approximately what it costs in electricity and propane per day to heat the pool. We do not make a profit on this fee.<br /><br />The home is approximately 1000 sq ft. <br /><br />The only way to access the home is by dirt road. The dirt road begins about half a mile before reaching the home. The dirt road is maintained by the neighborhood, and any type of vehicle can drive on it. <br /><br />The third bedroom is in an open loft area, which has low ceilings, so please watch your head! <br /><br />The pool is 18 feet in diameter and ranges from 4.5-5.5 feet deep, and the spa is 6 feet in diameter. <br /><br />Please make sure to treat the furniture as if it were your own. Most of the furniture and decor is vintage and cannot be easily replaced. <br /><br />We are located in the desert with lots of native wildlife. Please be aware this includes snakes, mice, coyotes, insects, etc."
      }
