      "id": "DESCRIPTION_DEFAULT",
      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "Bungalow N°3 is a unique overwater bungalow featuring an open-flow living room and kitchen design, providing unobstructed 180° panoramic views of Bora Bora's famous lagoon. Once owned by Hollywood's own Jack Nicholson, this luxurious bungalow offers a slice of paradise. Relax on the terrace, bask in the cool ocean breezes, swim in the lagoon, watch the setting sun, or marvel at the nightly animation of fish swimming around the underwater lights.<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />Overwater Bungalow 3 does evoke an aura of dreamy indulgence! Its combination of modern amenities and natural beauty creates a perfect balance for a relaxing vacation. The panoramic view from the living room, framed by the expansive floor-to-ceiling sliding glass doors, invites a breathtaking vista of the lagoon beyond. A snug sofa accompanied by a television and Apple TV offers a cozy spot for unwinding and entertainment. Indulge in the culinary creations in the  impeccably equipped modern kitchen. Marble tile flooring adds a touch of luxury to the space. <br /><br />The bedroom is a cozy haven with its king size bed and ample storage, perfect for unwinding after a day of exploring. The inclusion of a large work space is convenient for those who need to catch up on work or stay connected, while the addition of a television and Apple TV provides entertainment options.<br /><br />The highlight undoubtedly lies in the spacious, shaded terrace, blessed with gentle breezes and  teak slats providing unmatched comfort for al fresco dining, leisurely reading, or simply unwinding. Here, guests can relax, savor peaceful meals, read or play a game of cards while  observing the ebb and flow of the day, with outrigger boats and other vessels passing by. The lower sun deck is the perfect vantage point to bask in the sun's warmth by day, perhaps even taking a refreshing dip for some snorkeling adventures. And as evening falls, the underwater fish lights cast a magical glow, transforming dinner into an unforgettable and truly enchanting experience.<br /><br /> Overwater Bungalow 3 offers a tranquil oasis where guests can unwind, rejuvenate, and craft cherished memories that will linger long after their stay.<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />The bungalow is located at the end of a long dock, positioned as the middle bungalow among five. It is clearly marked as Bungalow N3. You will have exclusive access to the entire downstairs floor of the bungalow. The dock and walkways are spacious, with no stairs hindering interior access, making it wheelchair-friendly. Upon check-in, you will receive the lockbox code to access the house keys as per the provided instructions. Additionally, free parking is available on the roadside.<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />Restaurants & Dining:<br /><br />Lunch service typically begins at 11:30 am and ends between 1:30 pm and 2:00 pm in Polynesia.<br />Staff typically rest after lunch service and return around 6:00 pm for dinner service, which usually ends by 9:30 pm.<br />Reservations are advised for dinner service.<br />Alcohol Regulations:<br /><br />In French Polynesia, alcohol sales are forbidden after 8:00 pm from Monday to Saturday and after 12 noon on Sundays.<br />Restaurants are permitted for alcohol consumption with dining.<br />Additionally, alcohol sales are closed on national holidays and election days.<br />Liquorl is costly in French Polynesia; consider purchasing it duty-free before arrival.<br /><br /><b>Registration number</b><br />1052DTO-MT"
