      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "If you are looking for a villa that has soul and style this could be the place for you. Near our restaurant  YELLOW FLOWER CAFE,Ubud.<br />Island to Island is our I G for more photos.<br /> Whether you are planning an intimate retreat , a special getaway or an exotic honeymoon we have you covered with this idyllic property. Click on my profile PHOTO to see our other exceptional villa and the reviews about us.<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />About this villa.<br /><br />*A few minutes walk to  many of Ubuds best cafes,galleries, temples,shops,spas,yoga and restaurants.<br />*Totally private villa and pool.<br />*Huge comfy super king size bed.<br />*Safe and secure.<br />*Wifi internet <br />*Open plan luxury tropical villa so not suitable for anyone with a bug or nature phobia but please note bugs here are same as anywhere in Bali.<br />*Yes,we can organise all your transport needs.<br />*Yes,we can deliver food from our cafe the Yellow Flower Cafe or a floating breakfast for the pool, flowers in the pool or flower bath or special decorations for honeymoon or romantic getaway. Flowers placed throughout the villa on arrival are included.<br />#Ubud Palace and Market 1.3km<br />Campuhan Ridge Walk 550 meters<br />Ubud Monkey Forest 3.2km<br />#Not suitable for anyone with a mobility issue as you must WALK INTO THIS VILLA a few minutes on an unpaved path. A car cannot drop you at the door. <br />To walk to the main road of Ubud is a few minutes walk and there are many steps to climb. A motor bike can be parked 1 minute walk away. We carry your luggage for you on check-in and check-out.<br />*Check-in before 9pm please.<br /><br />This boutique one-of-a-kind villa is built around the pillars of a 200 year old antique  joglo. It exudes rustic elegance and has a sophisticated charm that will delight the sense and bring on the romance for a truly exotic holiday or honeymoon. <br /><br /><br />The joglo roof is the most complex of all Javanese roof types.  Joglo roof consists of columns that become higher as it goes to the center. The four innermost main house columns are often the tallest, while the outer columns are the lowest. These four innermost house columns support a roof that is the steepest of all type of Javanese roof; almost forming a pyramid, except that it comes to two points rather than a single one. These four innermost main house columns is surmounted by a unique structural element known as tumpang sari. A tumpang sari is basically layered beams structure; the outermost band of beams support the rafters of both the upper and lower roofs, while the heavily-ornate inner band of beams create a vaulted ceiling in the form of an inverted stepped pyramid.<br /><br /><br />Traditionally, joglo roof is used for the house proper (omah) or the pavilion (pendopo) of noble families. In a large house compound of a Javanese noble family, joglo roof covers the very center part of the house. The space in the middle of the house, known as the dalem, is considered the most sacred. This sacred space – especially the area beneath the tumpang sari – is often left empty. In modern time, the area has no specific usage, but traditionally an incense was burnt once a week in this area to honor the rice goddess Dewi Sri, or in Central Java, to honor Nyai Roro Kidul.This sacred area is also the area where the bride and bridegroom are seated during their marriage ceremony.<br /><br />The joglo roof is an iconic Javanese roof form. Joglo roof has influenced the development of Dutch colonial architecture in Indonesia...<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />This villa is ideally situated down a leafy path in a quite Balinese community. It is away from traffic and in walking distance to many of Ubuds best bits. If you dont want to walk there is a scooter hire place near by or drivers on stand-by at the bottom of the steps. To get to ubud you must walk down many steps unless you have a motor bike then you can park at the top.<br /> Also the path to the villa is not perfectly paved so you may need to watch your step.<br />We can arrange any transport for you. If you need airport pick up please give us name and all flight details so we can copy and paste to one of our friendly drivers.<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />#We provide reliable fast Wifi internet.<br /><br /><br />#At some times of the year there may be some mosquitoes especially at around 6pm. We provide repellent and mosquito coils to keep them away. You can also bring your own personal repellent.<br /><br />#The villa is open plan tropical living so at times there might be some criters likes frogs, yellow belly garden lizard or insects. For anyone who has a nature phobia this might not be the place for you. Only the master bedroom and bathroom is fully enclosed and a/c.<br /><br />#The walk in is not  fully paved for. There are many stairs to get to the main road of Ubud but easily accessible for most travellers, however if you have mobility issues or are not comfortable walking it may not be suitable. Like many villas and resorts in Bali must walk in a few minutes and the walk in keeps the area blissfully free of traffic noise and pollution. You can walk in 4 different directions from the villa or ride a motor bike and park 1 minutes walk away. We carry your bags for you on check-in and check-out.<br /><br />#In Bali it is important to us that we place offerings in every dwelling every day. We will do this in the day when we clean. <br /><br />#Sorry but this property is not safe or suitable for children under 12.<br /><br /># Not suitable for anyone with a mobility issue.<br /><br />#We can store your luggage  at our cafe for free  till 9pm on the day of your check out if need be. Or you can leave bags from 7am before you check in.<br /><br /># We have a new I G account  called   island to island .See our feed for more images. Also check out our restaurant Yellow Flower Cafe. We only accept bookings via airbnb."
      }
