    {
      "id": "DESCRIPTION_DEFAULT",
      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "Fully refurbished in 2025 including new furnishings, kitchen, bathroom, floors, artworks, appliances, dinnerware, linen, etc. You can't really get a better location than this cosy apartment. It is located beside Grafton Street and Trinity College and nestled in the very heart of the most exclusive & historic district of Dublin's city centre. Our guests love our welcome pack which includes guides on our favourite pubs, restaurants, cafe's, sights and more.<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />This fantastic just newly refurbished  1 bedroom, 1 bathroom apartment comes with a free car parking space and is located on one of the quieter side streets in the city centre. The apartment itself contains a spacious double bedroom with Umage light fittings and a designer bathroom by the 'Bathroom Boutique' with shower and toilet facilities. There is a fully fitted bespoke kitchen by 'Kube' (with dishwasher, oven, microwave, fridge/freezer, crockery, cookware, glassware, all  utensils, etc) and a cosy living/dining room with designer furniture and a LG smart TV on a 3D extendable bracket.  Original Ciaran Meister paintings adorn the walls (Nominated as British Artist of the Year 2024). Please note there is no elevator in the building and this apartment is located up a set of stairs on the 1st floor.<br /><br />Bedroom - King sized bed (2 persons - 150cm x 200cm)<br />Living room - King 'plus' Sofa bed (2 persons - 160cm x 200cm)<br /><br />The Perfect location!  All these major attractions are a short walk away:<br /><br />> Within 5 mins walk: Grafton Street, Trinity College, St Stephens Green, The Book of Kells & Old Library, Irish Whiskey Museum, National Museum of Ireland (Archaeology), National Library of Ireland and National Gallery of Ireland.<br /><br />> Within 10 mins walk: Temple Bar Area, Harcourt Street Area, Merrion Square, Gaiety Theatre and Little Museum of Dublin.<br /><br />> Within 15 mins walk: O'Connell Bridge, Irish Rock n Roll experience, Ha'penny Bridge, Camden Street Area, Chester Beatty Library, Dublin Castle and the GPO Museum.<br /><br />> Within 20 mins walk: Christ Church Cathedral, Epic Irish Emigration Museum, National Leprechaun Museum Ireland, Marsh's Library, Saint Patricks Cathedral and The Jeanie Johnston Famine Ship.<br /><br />The apartment is professionally cleaned after every guest and freshly laundered bed sheets and towels come as standard with each booking. The bedrooms have hotel grade mattresses, duvets & pillows and the bedding is 100% cotton with high thread count of minimum 200 threads per square inch.<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />The entire apartment is for your exclusive use only.<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />We have carefully crafted detailed arrival instructions as well as a wide variety of tips/advice for the apartment, local area and Dublin city in general! We have put a lot of effort into these documents and improve them on a regular basis."
      }
