    {
      "id": "DESCRIPTION_DEFAULT",
      "htmlDescription": {
        "htmlText": "Welcome to Hangar Nine, a cozy retreat on the outskirts of Nairobi, offering a peaceful escape from city life. Situated on a family-owned small holding farm just an hour's drive from downtown Nairobi or the Jomo Kenyatta International Airport, the house features three bedrooms, two bathrooms, an open plan living area, a large veranda, a swimming pool and a sundowner fire pit from which to unwind and take in views of the Nairobi city skyline in the distance.<br /><br /><b>The space</b><br />*Please ensure you have the correct number of people in your booking for the correct rate to apply. <br /><br />Inside, you'll find a laid-back open-plan living area, combining a kitchen, dining space, and lounge for easy living. The house is stocked with almost every amenity you should need including various cooking utensils, fridges, cooker, a TV and more. <br /><br />Three bedrooms offer comfortable accommodation: the master bedroom features an ensuite bathroom with a shower and bath and a king-size bed wrapped in a romantic mosquito net. Adjacent, two additional bedrooms offer flexible accommodation options, sharing a convenient Jack and Jill bathroom. The green room features another sumptuous king-sized bed, while the yellow room offers versatility with twin beds that can be combined into a double, accommodating various guest preferences.<br /><br />Outside, the veranda beckons with a seating area and outdoor dining table overlooking the garden and swimming pool, with the Nairobi skyline in the distance. <br /><br />And when you're ready to explore, Nairobi National Park, the David Sheldrick Elephant Orphanage, the Giraffe Centre and Kitengela Glass are all within a 30-minute drive from Hangar Nine. Being on the edge of the city most restaurants are also a 30-minute or more drive away from the house however there is the option of having a cook during your stay for a small extra fee. <br /><br />Whether you're seeking a peaceful retreat or an adventure-filled getaway, Hangar Nine promises an unforgettable stay where nature and comfort converge. Come experience the beauty and serenity of Nairobi's outskirts at this exceptional Airbnb retreat.<br /><br />*Please note that we don't allow drop-ins or additional people beyond what is booked in your reservation.<br /><br /><b>Guest access</b><br />You will have access to the entire house, garden and pool area during your stay with us.<br /><br /><b>Other things to note</b><br />Hangar Nine is located on the edge of Nairobi and offers a wonderful escape from the hustle and bustle of the city. However, this does mean that if you are looking for nights out in town or meals at restaurants in the evening this may not be the ideal location for your holiday - the house has been designed as a retreat and escape from city life and there is an option of a cook for a small extra fee during your stay if you wish. <br /><br />Being located on a small holding farm the road up to the house is a little rough & rocky, but is accessible with most vehicles (if you are concerned please don't hesitate to get in touch) and you may see some goats and cows in the area however they don't come close to the house.<br /><br />Please note that we don't allow drop-ins or additional people beyond what is booked in your reservation so please ensure that you have the correct number of people in the system when booking thank you"
      }
